---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FdpCalculator from '../islands/FdpCalculator.tsx';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FDP calculator"
  description="Work out the maximum flight duty period for a 703/704/705 operation under CARs 700.28, with the augmented-crew (700.60) and split-duty (700.50) adjustments. Shows which table and rule it used."
>
  <div class="container calc-page">
    <header class="calc-page__head">
      <p class="calc-page__eyebrow">CARs 700.28 · 703 / 704 / 705</p>
      <h1>Maximum Flight Duty Period calculator</h1>
      <p class="calc-page__lede">
        Enter your report time, the number of flights and their average length, and your crew setup.
        The result shows the maximum FDP and exactly which table row and rule produced it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <FdpCalculator client:load />

    <section class="calc-page__notes prose">
      <h2>What it covers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The 700.28(2)/(3)/(4) duration tables and the 700.28(9) day-VFR table.</li>
        <li>
          Acclimatization — if you're not acclimatized, it reads the table using the local time in
          the zone you're still acclimatized to (700.28(5); AC 700-047 § 4.22).
        </li>
        <li>The 700.60 augmented-crew table (replaces the base maximum).</li>
        <li>The 700.50 split-duty extension: (break − 45 min) × 100% or 50%.</li>
        <li>The absolute 18-hour ceiling (700.62(1)).</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What it doesn't</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Positioning (<a href="/rules/700-43">700.43</a>), delayed reporting time (<a
            href="/rules/700-52">700.52</a
          >), consecutive-FDP limits (<a href="/rules/700-51">700.51</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          The <a href="/rules/700-40">rest period</a> that follows, or the disruptive-schedule / time-zone
          rest add-ons (<a href="/rules/700-41">700.41</a>,
          <a href="/rules/700-42">700.42</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          Unforeseen operational circumstance extensions — those are the pilot-in-command's call (<a
            href="/rules/700-63">700.63</a
          >).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .calc-page {
    padding-block: 2.25rem 1rem;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }
  .calc-page__eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }
  .calc-page__head h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .calc-page__lede {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .calc-page__notes {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
